---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Arranging a funeral', url: '/arranging-a-funeral/' }];
---

<Page
  title="Arranging a Funeral in Dunbar & East Lothian"
  heading="Arranging the funeral"
  description="What happens when you sit down with us to arrange a funeral in Dunbar: the decisions involved, how long it takes, and what you will be asked."
  standfirst="One conversation, at your pace. Twenty minutes or two hours — both are fine, and we have no timetable."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    Arranging a funeral is mostly a conversation. We will ask what the person was like,
    what they would have wanted, and what matters to you. Everything practical follows
    from that. You do not need to arrive having decided anything.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we meet</h2>
  <p>
    At our funeral home in Dunbar, or at your own home if you would rather not go
    anywhere. A lot of families find it easier at their own kitchen table, and we are
    happy to come to you anywhere in East Lothian or Berwickshire.
  </p>

  <h2>What we will talk about</h2>

  <h3>Burial or cremation</h3>
  <p>
    If the person left no instruction, this is usually the first decision. Neither is more
    correct than the other, and cost is a legitimate part of the decision.{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-services/burial/">Burial</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-services/cremation/">cremation</a> are both explained in more
    detail, along with{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-services/natural-burial/">natural burial</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-services/direct-cremation/">direct cremation</a> if you would like
    something simpler.
  </p>

  <h3>Where and when</h3>
  <p>
    A church, the crematorium chapel, a graveside, our own funeral home, or somewhere
    that meant something to them. We will check what is available and work around family
    who need to travel. We have written up{' '}
    <a href="/directory/crematoria/">what to expect at each of the local crematoria</a>{' '}
    if it helps to picture it.
  </p>

  <h3>Who will lead the service</h3>
  <p>
    A minister, a priest, a humanist or independent celebrant, or a member of the family.
    We know the local ministers and celebrants well and will suggest someone we think
    will suit you. There is no obligation to have anyone at all.
  </p>

  <h3>The coffin</h3>
  <p>
    We carry the full range from Ecoffins — willow, bamboo, banana leaf, pandanus, and
    fully recycled cardboard — alongside traditional wooden coffins. You can{' '}
    <a href="/coffins/">see the whole range</a> before you come in, so it is not a
    decision made cold in front of a catalogue.
  </p>

  <h3>Everything else</h3>
  <p>
    Cars, flowers, notices in the local papers, orders of service, music, donations in
    lieu, a reception afterwards, and what happens to the ashes. Some families want all
    of it and some want none. Both are perfectly normal.
  </p>

  <Callout title="What you will not be asked to do">
    <ul>
      <li>Decide anything on the spot</li>
      <li>Sign anything at the first meeting</li>
      <li>Justify a budget</li>
      <li>Explain why you do or do not want something</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Costs</h2>
  <p>
    We will give you a written estimate covering everything discussed, itemised, before
    you commit to anything. You are welcome to take it home and think about it, or to
    compare it with another funeral director — we would rather you were sure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/standardised-price-list/">Standardised Price List</a> is
    published here, displayed in our window and available in print. If money is a worry,
    say so early — there is often{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/help-with-funeral-costs/">more help available</a> than people
    expect, and we will help you get it.
  </p>

  <h2>Seeing the person who has died</h2>
  <p>
    You can visit whenever you would like, for as long as you would like, and as often as
    you would like. If you want to help dress them or place something in the coffin, you
    can. If you would rather remember them as they were, that is right too. Nobody will
    think anything of either choice.
  </p>

  <h2>On the day</h2>
  <p>
    We will be there from the start and will stay until everyone has gone. Our job is to
    take every practical worry off you so that you can be present with your family
    instead of managing the arrangements.
  </p>

  <h2>Afterwards</h2>
  <p>
    We will help with ashes, memorials, headstones and the paperwork that keeps arriving
    for months. And if you simply want to come in for a blether some weeks later, the
    door is open — a lot of people do, and it is never an imposition.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      To arrange a time to meet, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a> or{' '}
      <a href="/contact/">send us a message</a>.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Page>
